{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1168530-naming-my-campaign-podcast","id":1168530,"title":"Naming My Campaign/Podcast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-18T08:37:49-08:00","id":1168530,"title":"Naming My Campaign/Podcast","content":"This is a cross post from the Whitewolfrpg subreddit, so it references a thread there, but the question/problem should stand on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Changeling The Dreaming campaign that I mentioned that I was planning on the &quot;What is your game about&quot;thread is having its first session tomorrow. We're also planning on recording it and releasing it as a podcast; or at least trying to since we've never recorded or performed our sessions before.<br /> <br /> I normally don't bother giving my campaigns titles, but since it will also be a podcast as well, this time I need to give this thing a cool title.<br /> <br /> The basic pitch of the campaign is in the above mentioned thread so I won't repeat the general details, but I will give some of the story specifics to see if any kind, creative soul can help me out.<br /> <br /> The game's setting is a large K-12 school in an undisclosed North American city (I'm thinking South Eastern Canada, New England or the North East states like Minnesota or Michigan but ultimately the specific location is going to be unstated). The school, Midfield Academy, is a microcosm of Channeling commoner society and each wing of the school serves as a different county with a different subculture and manifestation of Chimerical reality. Some places like the gifted program wing are bright and wondrous, while others like the alternative program for severe behavioural issues are hellish nightmare scapes.<br /> <br /> The players are mostly students, save for the one adult who is the assistant librarian. They all have disappointing and difficult mortal lives, so they invest themselves in the Chimerical side of life at Midfield, going on adventures and helping staff and students in need. They are often pulled back to reality by the horrible and traumatic events in their own lives and those of their peers. It is a campaign about drastically shifting tones, juxtaposition and dualities.<br /> <br /> The first adventure is a three act story that begins as a fun Christmas themed quest where the Nocker Science teacher send them on a quest to find a piece of Chimerical machinery that he needs to put on a Santa's Workshop in which students will be able to temporarily enter the Dreaming and live a &quot;real&quot; North Pole experience for a time during the school Christmas pageant. It turns out that a Chimera that is able to possess mortals and is modelled after Krampus has taken the machine piece because he wants to use it to find a way to enter the Autumn world and punish all the kids on his naughty list. &quot;Krampus&quot; tries to generate a bunch of nightmare themed Glamour by using his possession ability to force the school's mortals to hurt and abuse eachother.<br /> <br /> Act 2 will introduce a family of Thallain that come to join the school community. They originally come on as friends who help the player characters with their individual problems as well as the Krampus Chimera if the players aren't able to do so themselves. This act is all about exploring the personal lives and motivations of the player characters and building friendships with people that appear caring, but actually want to disarm the characters so that they can hurt them more later.<br /> <br /> Act 3 is when the Thallain begin to show their true colours. The ghast father begins cutting out and eating people's organs, the goblin little girl begins setting traps that maim and kill people in horrible and graphic ways, the ogre kid begins pushing the put upon immigrant boy into violently lashing out at everyone who mistreats him, etc. This act is about betrayal of trust and the players' reactions to it.<br /> <br /> So what should I call this Campaign and what should I call this story?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}